Step 1: Firewall & Security Group Preparation
Ensure both Port 80 (HTTP) and Port 443 (HTTPS) are open in the AWS EC2 Security Group (0.0.0.0/0)
and the Linux host UFW firewall:

# Allow HTTP and HTTPS traffic through host firewall
sudo ufw allow 80/tcp comment 'HTTP Web Ingress'
sudo ufw allow 443/tcp comment 'HTTPS Encrypted Ingress'
sudo ufw reload

Step 2: Configure Public DNS A Record
Navigate to your Domain Registrar or DNS Manager (Route53, Cloudflare, Namecheap, DuckDNS, No-IP) 
and map your domain to your EC2 instance's Public IP:

Record Type         | Host / Name                             | Target / Value                                                        | TTL          |
|---------------------|-----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|
| A                   | @ (or app)                              | <YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP>                                                  | 300 (5 mins) |

Verify DNS Propagation
Run dig or nslookup from your local terminal to confirm your domain points to your EC2 IP address:

##Proceed once the query returns your server's public IP!

Step 3: Update Nginx Virtual Host Configuration
Connect to your server via SSH and update /etc/nginx/sites-available/load-balancer to replace generic wildcards with your domain name:

sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/load-balancer

server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;

    # Explicit domain target for ACME validation
    server_name mytestsever.myftp.biz;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://node_backend_pool;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}

Verify syntax and reload Nginx:

sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx


Step 4: Install Certbot & Trigger ACME Automation
Install Certbot along with its dedicated Nginx integration module:

# Install Certbot & Nginx plugin
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y certbot python3-certbot-nginx

# Execute automated certificate issuance & Nginx configuration
sudo certbot --nginx -d app.yourdomain.com

During the Interactive Setup:

Email Prompt: Provide a sysadmin email address for urgent renewal/security alerts.


Terms of Service: Agree to the Let's Encrypt Terms (Y).


HTTPS Redirect: Select Option 2 to force all plain HTTP (Port 80) traffic to redirect to HTTPS (Port 443) automatically.
